Chapter 3: My University Journey

Beginning My Higher Education

After moving from Liberia to Rwanda, I began a new chapter of my academic journey at the University of Lay Adventists of Kigali (UNILAK).

My decision to pursue higher education was driven by my desire to gain knowledge, develop practical skills, and prepare myself for a better future.

As a Software Engineering student, I became increasingly interested in programming, computer systems, technology, and innovation.

University life has introduced me to new challenges, responsibilities, and opportunities to grow academically and personally.

I understand that becoming a successful professional requires commitment, discipline, continuous learning, and determination.

My university journey is still in progress, and I remain committed to learning, improving, and preparing for the opportunities ahead.

My goal is not simply to earn a degree, but to acquire knowledge and skills that will allow me to make a meaningful contribution to society.
